      {
         "id": "SECTION_introdução",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Introduction\n\nWriting appeared in Sumeria around <htdate0>. At first, it was pictographic. That means people drew symbols that remind us of something, like objects. Later, writing moved to a method that reproduces sounds: phonetic writing (<htcite0>). However, the fact that writing appeared in Sumeria does not mean other peoples copied it. Different writing systems appeared in other places, completely on their own (<htcite1>).\n\nWriting represents the sounds we make. So, logically, the sounds came first. This leads us to our first reflection.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "73c1fc70-769e-47cb-a7b4-597a73d21a93",
                     "text": "Dr. Irving Finkel",
                     "page": "00:05:20 - 11:40",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2019",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "5390fa3b-735f-4e22-ac98-178303a13fdb",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "The Writing System",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "-3400",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection question_mark\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-brain\"></i></div><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\"><b>Reflection 1: Is it necessary?</b><br /><br />Would all the peoples of the planet have created a writing system?<br /><br />Or did some not feel the need to do so and, even so, manage to transmit knowledge?</div></div></center>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_voice",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### When did the voice emerge?\n\nSpeech, as we know it, happens because of morphological differences. These are changes in the human body compared to other animals. They may have helped speech appear in our species (<htcite0>).\n\nArticulated speech is a human feature. But other primates also have a voice. For example, chimpanzees (**Figure 1**), orangutans, and primates in general (<htcite1>).",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "da4b4f3a-f48c-4c17-87ca-0ebad8ba1165",
                     "text": "Belin, P.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2006",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "da4b4f3a-f48c-4c17-87ca-0ebad8ba1165",
                     "text": "Belin, P.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2006",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"imgChimp\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgChimp', '0%')\" src=\"\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 1</b>: Image of chimpanzees in their natural habitat. © Taï Chimpanzee Project (<htcite0>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "abbf6d09-8755-46b6-b6fb-506c81549605",
                     "text": "Taï Chimpanzee Project",
