      {
         "id": "SECTION_teaching",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Oral Knowledge Transmission\n\nWe, *Homo sapiens*, appeared on Earth at least 300,000 years ago. Other species of the genus Homo appeared about 2,000,000 years ago (<htcite0>; <htcite1>).\n\nWriting is recent when we compare it to our speciation process. Speciation is the process in which new species appear over generations, as changes build up. So, for a long time, knowledge was passed on through speech.\n\nWe can see oral transmission of knowledge and traditions for centuries among the Shona people of Zimbabwe. They did this through the organization and structure of their kitchens (**Figure 2**) (<htcite2>; <htcite3>).",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "8b0527b7-cf08-4e3b-8148-347cd178e607",
                     "text": "Tuttle, R.H.",
                     "page": "Human Evolution",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "1",
                        "day": "23"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "ab1dda1e-95c2-4087-8299-e851e58bdc6f",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Humans",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "cc162709-bdc3-469b-a208-e900f4570842",
                     "text": "Sadomba, Zvakanyorwa Wilbert",
                     "page": "pp. 244 - 248",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "1c6f4dce-a58a-4c06-b4a8-6f509575f42a",
                     "text": "Muratu, Brian Z.",
                     "page": "pp. 56",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img src=\"\" id=\"imgShona\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgShona', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 2</b>: Photos of the Shona kitchen. At the top left, we see a photo of the kitchen with the door closed. At the top right, we see the back of the kitchen. At the bottom, there are images of the interior of the building. These photos were taken by Brian Z. Muratu (<htcite0>) and are being used under the terms defined by the University of Johannesburg, which shared the dissertation under the <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\">Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike</a> license.</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "1c6f4dce-a58a-4c06-b4a8-6f509575f42a",
                     "text": "Muratu, Brian Z.",
                     "page": "pp. 56",
                     "date_time": {
